    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d522">

                <pb facs="0632" n="1466" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1466"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/396</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Netherland Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">De
                        Beaufort</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 20, 1918</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to
                    inform Your Excellency that in order to be able to answer in an unqualified
                    manner the doubts expressed in all directions concerning the intentions of the
                    Associated Governments, my Government has instructed me to ask the American
                    Government to be good enough to give me the formal assurance that from the 20th
                    of last March no vessel flying the Dutch flag will be seized or detained in a
                    port of the United States.</p>
                <p>In consequence of the foregoing, I have the honor to have recourse to the
                    obliging good offices of Your Excellency in order to obtain as soon as possible
                    from the Government of the United States the assurance asked for by my
                    Government.</p>
                <p>In thanking Your Excellency in advance for the attention which you will be good
                    enough to give to my request, I take this opportunity to renew the assurances of
                    my highest consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. de Beaufort</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
